  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Gemini Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving into implementing the `GeminiService`. I intend to use the Direct REST API pattern in Kotlin with Room integration. I\'ve paused to review the `gemini-api` skill\'s requirements for the service. Key is initializing the Retrofit client to the base URL and handling response/error conditions.\n\n\n**Refining Payload Structures**\n\nI\'ve decided to refine the payload models. I\'m leveraging Moshi annotations to construct JSON representations of requests and responses. It looks straightforward given our current project setup. The `kotlinx-serialization` plugin isn\'t applied, so Moshi or standard code becomes ideal for direct REST calls. Given the Gemini model accepts standard JSON, simple OkHttp requests with JSON bodies or standard Retrofit/Moshi are easy. The endpoint is still in review.\n\n\n**Designing Gemini Service Functionality**\n\nI\'m now outlining the core features of `GeminiService`. The design prioritizes three primary functions: OCR analysis and medicine extraction from images, detection of medicine interactions given a current medicine list and a new medicine, and dosage suggestions with associated safety rules. I\'m focusing on crafting a robust implementation, including a prompt for the Gemini model (`gemini-3.5-flash`) to ensure structured JSON responses for the `PrescriptionExtractionResponse` format. This setup allows real calls if the API key is present or falls back to simulated data, which feels optimal.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/app/src/main/java/com/example/data/ai/GeminiService.kt` to handle our real AI features. It will parse and process medical prescriptions using Gemini (`gemini-3.5-flash` model), perform optical character recognition (OCR) with structured JSON responses, run drug-to-drug safety interaction analysis, detect duplicates, and generate schedule suggestions. It is designed to automatically utilize the key from AI Studio secrets and fall back to graceful, high-quality simulated data if no key is supplied."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 331029979
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
