  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Appreciating Core Architecture**\n\nI\'m incredibly impressed. This repository perfectly embodies the principles of Clean Architecture and offline-first design. I\'m especially excited by the Room database implementation, the REST API interfaces with Retrofit, Gemini OCR integration, and the dynamic pricing. The admin configuration and family records also seem well-simulated. It\'s a remarkably comprehensive approach.\n\n\n**Defining ViewModel Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the structure of `MediReminderViewModel`, considering essential elements. I\'ll need to manage user authentication, the medicines list from the repository, a reactive daily schedule tied to the selected calendar day, and the state of prescription uploads and OCR processing. I\'m also including interaction warnings, compliance metrics, and simulating admin state variables for live synchronization scenarios.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/viewmodel/MediReminderViewModel.kt` to house the ViewModel that acts as the single source of truth for our dynamic Compose UI. It computes real-time compliance metrics, coordinates prescription scanning states, analyzes duplicate medication risks and safety warnings via the Gemini API, simulates real-time administration commands (blocking, alerts, maintenance mode, pricing updates), and handles family record registries."
