  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Crafting Main App Screen**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the Compose screens. To avoid any immediate compiler headaches, I\'m setting up a `MainAppScreen.kt` file within the `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/screens/` directory. This should provide a clean and organized starting point for these screens.\n\n\n**Designing App Layout**\n\nI\'ve decided to build the entire interactive layout within `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/screens/MediReminderAppLayout.kt`. This will house all the necessary screens, keeping things tidy and architecturally sound. I\'m prioritizing the layout and now fleshing out the specific screens: blocked, maintenance, and login. I\'m focusing on their interactive elements and visual designs for a better user experience.\n\n\n**Building Dashboard Screen**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the dashboard screen design. I\'m prioritizing dynamic greetings and interactive \"Blocked/Price\" settings. I\'ve integrated an admin simulation panel for real-time data validation, and I\'m developing a responsive, custom circular ring displaying compliance percentages. Today\'s doses are now organized with click actions and time markers, along with active medicine cabinets. I\'m also preparing the admin notifications banner.\n\n\n**Developing Prescription Capture Flow**\n\nI\'m now deep in the prescription capture workflow. The user can either snap an image or simulate picking one from the gallery. This triggers a call to `GeminiService.extractPrescription(...)`. The process then verifies the results by displaying extracted timings and medicine cards, allowing for edits, and duration adjustments. Tapping \"Confirm\" saves everything to Room. Next, I\'m building the manual entry screen, with form fields for name, dosage, and frequency.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/screens/MediReminderAppLayout.kt` to define our modern Material Design 3 user experience. It will feature responsive container sizes, an Admin Simulation HUD (so you can test blocked accounts, maintenance mode, global message broadcasts, and dynamic price edits live!), custom circular progress canvases, calendar day cards, camera uploading, and prescription parsing with drug safety checks."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 426643508
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
